 "post": {
  "title": "One Letter Made People Happier for a Month #shorts",
  "description": "Omar thinks thank-you notes are for weddings, so Grace hands him a pen. The gratitude visit: write a letter to someone who changed your life and was never properly thanked, then read it to them in person. In 2005 Martin Seligman, Tracy Steen, Nansook Park and Christopher Peterson (\"Positive Psychology Progress\", American Psychologist) tested several happiness exercises online; the gratitude visit produced the biggest boost in happiness, still visible a month later, though it had faded by six months. So: write another one. #psychology #shorts #gratitude #happiness",
